 { component: 'MV HDD bores', scope: '20 bores', done: 19, pct: 95, weight: 25, contribution: 23.75, note: '9,050 ft. <strong>MVHB-10 IS COMPLETE at 1,794 ft \u2014 the first bore closed since Aug 13 and the end of a front that recorded ZERO feet for two weeks.</strong> The ITS tracker logs it finished 23 Aug and it appears on the Aug 25 cut. <strong>Bores go 18 \u2192 19 of 20 and MVHB-11 moves from Pending to In progress</strong>, so a single trunk crossing is now the whole of the remaining drilling scope. MV composite rises 74.7 \u2192 75.9 on this alone. The Wetland environmental record behind the Aug 19 event still has to be completed and filed.' },
 { component: 'DC duct bores', scope: '10 locations (4 of 14 cancelled)', done: 10, pct: 100.0, weight: 15, contribution: 15.0, note: '<strong>SCOPE COMPLETE Aug 13 - 10 of 10 approved bores (DC-01 and DC-06 culminated)</strong>. PRIOR — DC bore 05 on Aug 7 and DC bore 14 (Area A) on Aug 8, the first units ITS has completed since Jul 30. 9 pending. Footage not yet filed for the two August bores; the 647 lf figure is the Jul 31 ITS control cut for the first three.' },
 { component: 'MV terminations', scope: '264 terminations', done: 15, pct: 5.7, weight: 15, contribution: 0.85, note: '<strong>SCOPE CORRECTED AND THE FRONT HAS OPENED. The new MV Termination Production Control puts the scope at 264 terminations across 46 units (23 inverters + 23 MV junction boxes), not the 138 carried here until now \u2014 a 91% increase in the count.</strong> <strong>6 are complete (2.3%), all at Inverters 01 and 02 in Area A, executed by AB Power on Aug 27.</strong> The same control gives the rest of the interface: <strong>trenches 58 open, 10 closed and 10 compacted of 181; cable pull-in complete at 7 of 46 units.</strong> Overall interface completion 10.7%. <strong>No unit is Complete on any line or in any area yet</strong> \u2014 a unit closes only when its trenches, pull-in and terminations are all done. <strong>The crew reached site on Aug 26 to start terminations and could not, because it did not bring the required tools.</strong> MV couplings still carry a ~40-week lead and the alternative sourcing plan is still owed.' }
